Z||000005||BN Boomer||12-28-2001||06:47 PM||||Why on earth would you go to all the trouble of hacking up two cabs like that and then have to weld them back together? Why not just remove the two door cab completely and then install the crew cab?||||reg||5
Z||000006||jimmybpei||12-28-2001||07:09 PM||||Believe it or not this was the quickes way.<BR>It only took us about 1 hour to get the crew cab off, besides i didnt want to get into all the wireing since the reg cab is an 80 and the crew cab was a 92. So they had totally diff. dashes.<P>way easier and quicker this way. This is what my guys doo everyday so the 2 cabs are put back together the proper way for strength. They arn't just butt welded.<P>Later. <BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jimmybpeisig_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
